# Intent: Train 5 item A, fluid faces. The eyes, lids, tilt and mouth of the default skin glide to where they are asked to be instead of jumping: one eased step per pass of the update loop (maipai_facefx_core.h: a = dt / (tau + dt), so a slow frame never overshoots). A lid closes in about 30 ms and opens in about 90 ms, so a blink is a blink and not a flash; the gaze eases in about 70 ms; the emotion tilt in about 110 ms; the eyes drift up to 3 pixels to a new place every 0.7 to 2.2 s, shared by both eyes. While the unit speaks the mouth follows the loudness of its own voice (a loudness tap on every block the audio output task plays, a noise gate, an eased curve, attack 38 ms and release 105 ms) instead of opening and shutting at random every 180 ms. The base update loop slept 100 ms WITH the screen lock held whenever the unit was not idle, which limited the screen to a few refreshes a second while it listened or spoke (measured: 8 passes a second, 6 refreshes a second); under the fluid face it does not. Costs no heap: a few floats per eye, one atomic and two ints for the speech level; the tap is one atomic read while nobody speaks.
# Placement: unit (the face runs on the robot, so it is fluid with Home down)
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/{default.h,eyes.cpp,mouth.cpp} of the StackChan main component (MIT) for the elements; firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/audio/audio_service.cc (MIT) for the tap; new files hal/maipai_facefx.cc, maipai_facefx.h and maipai_facefx_core.h
# Check after a flash: the face blinks with a short fade, the eyes drift a little when idle, the mouth opens with the loudness of the voice while it speaks and closes between words; with the bench build self.face.bench_run talk shows loop_per_s near 50 (the base measured 8) and more refreshes a second than the base; a mute or vision-off look still shows the shut eyes and flat mouth.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_FACE_FLUID (default y); off restores the stepped base behaviour, including the 100 ms sleep.
